@@ -3,3 +3,24 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## API
+
+### `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`
+
+Returns the value of `document` referred to by a JSON Pointer ([RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901)).
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": 1 }, "/a~1b");             // 1
+resolvePointer({ a: 1 }, "");                      // the whole document
+```
+
+It throws an `Error` when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer (it must be empty or start with `/`,
+and `~` must be followed by `0` or `1`), or when it does not resolve to a value of the document: missing
+member, array index out of range, `-` (the nonexistent element after the last), an index with a leading
+zero or sign, or a step into a scalar or `null`. Only the document's own members are followed, so
+`__proto__`, `constructor` and similar tokens never reach the prototype chain. The document is not
+modified. The URI fragment form (`#/foo`) is not supported.
